SUBJECT:
BN Contract No.BF-20579498, BNSF Railway and Grant Applicant
22905Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and B NSF for
the Reed Avenue Rail Crossing Elimination Project.
Purpose and Need:
Enclosed for your review and consideration is the22905Agreement between the
City of Cheyenne and BNSF.The City of Cheyenne is advancing the Reed Avenue
Corridor Rail Crossing Elimination Project aspart of the Federal Railroad
Administration'sFY23-24Railroad Crossing Elimination Program.As outlined in
federal statute(49 USC522905), the City must enter into a formal agreement with
BNSF Railway, the owner of the affected rail corridor, to obtain necessary rights and
permissions for project development, final design, andfuture construction activities.
The safety components for the project intend to:
Improve safety by eliminating multipleat-grade crossings.
Upgrade remaining crossings with pedestrian safety devices and
channel iz ation.
Restrict accessto therailroad through new corridor fencing.
Install storm drainage improvements to convey stormwater out of the
corridor.
The attached BNSF agreement(File No.BF-20602500) outlines these federal
funds.
Cost and Funding
to compensate BNSFfor use ofrailroad propertyand to establish project
coordination procedures througha Construction and Maintenance Agreement(C&M
Agreement).Any necessary funding forthe agreement(C&M)willikely come from
the 2017 Specific Purpose Option Tax (6th Penny) Reed Avenue Rail Corridor.BNSF
has indicated that this compensation is a one-time payment foruse of its
right-of-way for the Reed Avenue Corridor Project.
